\subsection{Sensitivity Analysis and Comparison of Hazard Rate Estimation Approaches}

In this section, we analyse the sensitivity of the filter dynamics with respect to model parameters. Moreover, we compare two estimation approaches for the hazard rate process, highlighting the impact of using different information flows.

\subsubsection{Sensitivity Analysis of the Filter Dynamics}
We examine the sensitivity of the filter dynamics in Equation \eqref{SDEFilterG} to changes in key parameters.
The numerical simulations are performed with arbitrarily chosen parameters to enhance the visual representation of different behaviours. Specifically, we set $\lambda=0.06$, $\mu_1=0.02$, $\pi=0$, and $T=60$, while varying $\beta$ and $\mu_2$ in the following scenarios:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Case A: $\beta = 1$ and $\mu_2=0.12$ (Figure \ref{fig:sub1})
