\section{Results}
\label{sec:6}
In this section, we report our findings by first providing an overview of results drawn from system interaction logs and CSI results (§\ref{sec:6.1}). Next, we present several use cases that illustrate how Constella's AI features support interconnected character creation (§\ref{sec:6.2}). We then report the tool’s impact on writers and their writing processes, with particular attention to its alignment with or changes to their existing practices and the preservation of authorial control (§\ref{sec:6.3}). Lastly, we present findings on participants’ expectations for using Constella when writing the entire full-length story, suggested improvements for supporting varied writing processes, and system limitations such as generation quality and insufficient support for narrative advancement (§\ref{sec:6.4}).

\subsection{Overview}
\label{sec:6.1}
    \subsubsection{System Interaction Log}
    \label{sec:6.1.1}
    \autoref{fig:systemlog} provides a timeline of the tasks participants completed and Constella's AI features they engaged with over a 7–8 day period. As illustrated, participants approached the tasks in varying orders and durations, aligning with their individual creative processes. In addition, many participants leveraged Constella beyond the scope of the assigned tasks, tailoring its features to meet their personal needs. This variability highlights both the flexibility of our task design and the adaptability of Constella, demonstrating how they both supported personalized and self-directed creative processes. We now present a deeper analysis of \autoref{fig:systemlog}, supplemented by data from system interaction logs and participants’ Constella accounts.

