\textbf{User:} I tasted a sweet candy for the first time ever on Earth.\\
\textbf{Assistant:} Dear Diary, \textcolor{gray}{//Chorong’s journal entry.} \newline
Today, I had the strangest and sweetest experience. After Binggu and I crash-landed on Earth, while Binggu was busy repairing the spaceship, I decided to wander around a bit. That’s when I stumbled upon a tiny, colorful shop. It was filled with all kinds of vibrant items that seemed to welcome me in. What caught my eye the most were the little colorful marbles inside a clear glass jar.\newline

Curious, I asked the shop owner what they were, and he told me they were something called "candy." He said that on Earth, people eat these to feel good and that they’re especially popular with children. My heart filled with anticipation. I mustered up the courage to buy one and put it in my mouth... and wow! It was a truly delightful experience.\newline

The moment it touched my tongue, a refreshing, citrusy flavor spread through my mouth, and as it slowly melted, a sweet taste followed. It’s hard to put into words, but it felt like I had a warm ray of sunlight in my mouth. For a moment, all the stress and tension from battles seemed to melt away.\newline

I wanted to give one to Binggu too, but he was too focused on fixing the gears. Still, I kept thinking, I want him to experience this moment too. Next time I get a chance, I’ll ask him to try candy with me.\newline

Life on Earth is so different from our resource-scarce Planet XYZ. Everything here is abundant, and there are so many wonderful things to discover. Each day is filled with fresh and exciting experiences. I’d love for my parents to taste things like this too someday. Hoping for peaceful and happy days ahead, I end today with a quiet smile.\newline

With love,\newline
Chorong
\end{flushleft}
