\textbf{Assistant:} Dear Diary, \textcolor{gray}{//Metal Monster’s journal entry.} \newline
Today was truly a strange day. I'm not quite sure how to describe it, but I put a small object in my mouth—something that was just... sweet. The humans on this peculiar planet called Earth refer to it as “candy.” I couldn’t help but let out a cynical laugh when I realized that, unlike me, nothing here shares my metallic nature. Then, as if unaware of my reaction, a human approached and held out their palm, offering me several small, round, colorful items.\newline

The colors were captivating. Unlike the dull gray of metal or the cool sharpness of steel, these candies dazzled me with rainbow hues. Curious about what this light and small object might be, I cautiously put one in my mouth. At first, the hard shell grated on my senses, but once I pierced through it, a deep sweetness reached my tongue and wrapped around me.\newline

As it melted in my mouth, I felt as if I were floating, weightless, forgetting gravity itself. For someone like me, who has lived only within the bounds of iron rules and regulations, it was a completely new experience. That slick sensation momentarily freed me from the pride of being a self-proclaimed king.\newline

In that moment, I wondered—if sweetness like this could maintain one’s rule, wouldn’t it be far more effective than the old ways of dread and violence? But of course, that thought itself posed a danger. It strayed too far from my very nature.\newline

Might there be a chilling truth behind this earthly sweetness? Until I uncover it, I cannot fully trust this candy. I must return to my true role. I need to prepare for the day when Binggu shows a more formidable side.\newline

— The Metal Monster

