 %   \int_{r<R} d^2x R^{12}_{12} = r\int_0^{2\pi}d\theta \frac{1}{2}\omega_\theta^{12} =  \frac{n}{2}\int_0^{2\pi}d\theta \partial_\theta \theta = \pi n.
%\end{equation}

With this gravitational version of the Aharonov-Bohm effect, the spin connection at $r=R$ does affect the Dirac operator spectrum.
As we have seen in the edge state spectrum localized at $r=R$ in Sec.~\ref{sec:TRI vortex}, the spin connection in the effective angular momentum $J$ [Eq.~\ref{eq:angular momentum operator}] is proportional to $n-1$ and the value modulo 2 determines if the Dirac operator can have zero modes or not.
