\subsection{Diffusion coefficients}
We computed diffusivity $D$ using the \textit{compute msd} command from LAMMPS and performing a linear fit of the $\textrm{MSD} = 6 D t$. 
 The uncertainty in the diffusion coefficient in our simulation is negligible and thus omitted.
 Diffusion coefficient from DPMD agrees with FPMD within the reported uncertainty. For example, at $T=7000$ \si{K}, $\rho=10.7$ \si{g/cm^3}, 14.0 from DPMD is comparable to  FPMD's 
13.0$\pm 1.3$ in unit of \si{nm^2/s} (see Table \ref{tab:viscosity}.
Even within first-principles results, a large discrepancy remains.
For example, at T=5000 K, 10.7 \si{g/cm^3}, Alf\`e et. al. \cite{Alfe2000}
gives  $7.0 \pm 0.7$ but Li et. al. \cite{Li2021} gives $5.42 \pm 0.49$.
Our diffusivity value $6.6$ \si{nm^2/s} falls within the range reported by first-principles results. 
