In this section, we recall the theory for the dynamics of multicomponent mixtures and introduce the notation following closely Ref.~\cite{Bauermann2022a}.



\subsection{Free energy and chemical potentials}


We consider an incompressible multicomponent mixture composed of $n$ species, each characterized by a volume fraction $\phi_\alpha$ (with $1\le i\le n$) and the solvent with volume fraction $\phi_0=1-\sum_{i=1}^n\phi_\alpha$. 
 The free energy is given as
\begin{equation}\label{eq:free_energy}
    F[f]=\int d^\text{d} x \, \left(  f  +  \sum_{i=1}^n\frac{\kappa_\alpha}{2\nu_\alpha}\left(\nabla\phi_\alpha \right)^2 \right) \, ,
\end{equation}
where $\kappa_\alpha$ characterizes the  contributions of gradients to the free energy which are related to surface tension and $\nu_\alpha$ is the molecular volume of the components and solvent.
The free energy density is
\begin{align}\label{eq:free_energy_compact}
f =k_BT\sum_{i=0}^n\frac{\phi_\alpha}{\nu_\alpha}\ln\phi_\alpha  + 
\sum_{\langle ij \rangle}\chi_{\alpha\beta}\phi_\alpha\phi_\beta +\sum_{i=0}^n\omega^0_\alpha\phi_\alpha\, ,
\end{align}
where the sum over $\langle ij \rangle$ runs over all components pairs (including the solvent), $\chi_{\alpha\beta}$ denotes the symmetric interaction parameter, with $\chi_{ii}=0$; $\omega^0_\alpha$ are the internal free energies and $k_B$ is the Boltzmann constant. Introducing the exchange activity coefficients,
the chemical potential $\mu_\alpha=\nu_\alpha \delta F/\delta \phi_\alpha$ reads
\begin{align}
\mu_\alpha=k_B T \ln  \left( \gamma_\alpha \phi_\alpha \right) + \omega_\alpha - \kappa_\alpha \nabla^2 \phi_\alpha \, ,
\label{eq:chem_pot}
\end{align}
where $\omega_\alpha$ is the reference chemical potential  defined in Eq.~\eqref{eq:reference_mu}, which is independent of $\phi$, $\gamma_\alpha \phi_\alpha$ is the exchange activity of components $\alpha$ relative to the solvent, and the activity coefficient $\gamma_\alpha$ is defined as 
\begin{align}
 {\gamma}_\alpha=\phi_0^{-\frac{\nu_\alpha}{\nu_0}}\exp\left[\frac{\nu_\alpha}{k_B T} \sum_{j=1}^n  (\chi_{\alpha\beta}-\chi_{i0}-\chi_{j0}) \phi_\beta  \right] \,.
 \label{eq:act_coef}
\end{align}
