    N_1'= N_1, & & N_3'=\alpha_{4} N_3 + \alpha_{2} \big( N_1 - \frac{(\beta_{1}-\beta_{5})(1-\beta_{1})} {\lambda} \big).
\end{array}$$

\end{prop}

\begin{proof} The proof is straightforward and follows similarly to the proof of Proposition \ref{prop3.2}.
\end{proof}



