(1) \textit{Efficient Semantic Alignment Across Heterogeneous Modalities.}
In multimodal communication scenarios such as human-machine interaction and autonomous systems, diverse task requests, including eye-tracking signals, voice and textual commands, can be jointly interpreted to support task-oriented transmission. We adopt semantic alignment techniques that project heterogeneous modalities into a shared representation space like Contrastive Language-Image Pre-training (CLIP) \cite{radford2021learning}, which align visual and textual data through contrastive learning. Effective mapping and alignment within a shared semantic space is fundamental to supporting downstream inference and task-oriented transmission. 

