    % \item Condition \ref{item:Q_jump_condition} on the jumps is clearly satisfied if $Q$ is a continuous semimartingale. 
    % \item \label{item:rem_taun} By inspecting the proof it is clear that the conclusion continues to hold if the stopping times $\tau_n$ are replaced by any sequence of stopping times whose almost sure limit is given by $\tau = \{t\geq0: P_i(t) = 0\}$.
\end{remark} 

