For $p \in (0,\infty)^d$ we define the functions 
\[\overline \bfp (p) = N_1p_1+\dots+N_dp_d, \qquad \mu_i(p) = \frac{N_ip_i}{\overline \bfp(p)}.\]
Next, given initial wealth $w > 0$, an initial price $P(0) = p^0 \in (0,\infty)^d$ and  a tuple $(t,p,J) \in [0,\infty) \times (0,\infty)^d \times \R^d$ we set
