To establish item \ref{item:long-only} we recall that the $\Gamma$ process of this additively functionally generated portfolio is given by \eqref{eqn:Gamma}. 
The first two terms on the right hand side of \eqref{eqn:Gamma} are nonnegative because $G(\cdot,\mu)$ is nonincreasing and $G(t,\cdot)$ is concave. The final term is always nonnegative yielding nonnegativity of $\Gamma$. Since $G(0,\mu(p^0)) \leq 1$ we have $V^Q(t) \geq G(t)$ establishing that $V^Q$ is nonnegative if $G$ is nonnegative. The nonnegativity of $Q_i$ now follows in the exact same way as in the proof of Proposition~\ref{prop:additive_frictionless}, which establishes \ref{item:long-only}. 

It now just remains to prove item \ref{item:positive_price}. Recalling the function $F_i$ defined in \ref{item:positive_price} we have for every $i$ from \eqref{eqn:additive_Q_explicit} and \eqref{eqn:Gamma} that
\begin{align*}
    Q_i(t)-Q_i(s)  = F_i(\mu(t))-F_i(\mu(s)) + \Gamma(t) - \Gamma(s),
\end{align*} 
 Hence, setting $\tau_n = \inf\{t \geq 0: F_i(\mu(t)) \geq\overline F_i - 1/n\}$ we see that 
\[Q_i(\tau_n) - \sup_{s \leq \tau_n} Q_i(s) \geq F_i(\tau_n)-\sup_{s \leq \tau_n} F_i(s) + \Gamma(\tau_n) - \sup_{s \leq \tau_n} \Gamma(s) = 0,\] where the final step followed from the definition of $\tau_n$ and the fact that $\Gamma$ is increasing. Let $\sigma = \lim_{n \to \infty} \tau_n$ and note that by condition \eqref{eqn:positive_condition} we have $\P$-a.s.\ that $\sigma \leq \inf\{t \geq 0: \mu_i(t) = 0 \}$. Since $P_i(t) = 0 \iff \mu_i(t) = 0$ on the set $\{0 < \overline \bfp(t) < \infty\}$ it follows from Proposition~\ref{prop:positive} and Remark~\ref{rem:positive} that $P_i$, and hence $\mu_i$, remains positive on $\{0 < \overline \bfp < \infty\}$.   This yields the characterization of the explosion time $\xi$ and completes the proof.
