 Let $\alpha = \alpha_1+\alpha_2$ and $\un{d} = \un{d}_1+\un{d}_2$ where $\alpha_i\neq 0$ and $\un{d}_i$ satisfy \eqref{eq:ovdd0} for their respective lengths explained in Remark \ref{rem:d1d2}. Furthermore, fix $\lambda_i$ for $i=1,2$ and denote the resulting stability conditions from \eqref{eq:barphi} by $\sig_1$ and $\sigma_2$ respectively. If $$\mu_{\Flag_k}\Big(\mN^{\sig_1}_{\un{d}_1,\alpha_1}\times \mN^{\sig_2}_{\un{d}_2,\alpha_2}\Big)\subset \mN^{\sig}_{\un{d},\al}\,,$$ then there should exist a homotopy commutative diagram 
