%up to homotopy. The first morphism is just the inclusion of the degree 4 term as a summand, and the second morphism can be represented by an actual morphism of complexes from $\mV ^*\otimes \mV\otimes H^\bullet(\mO_X)$ to a vector bundle. This follows after taking an injective resolution $O^\bullet$ of $\mO_{X\times \mN_k}$ on $X$ because there is a morphism $O^\bullet\to \mF(k)$ homotopy equivalent to $\mO_{X\times \mN_k}\to \mF(k)$ with both its source and target being acyclic for the derived pushforward along the projection $X\times \mN_k\to \mN_k$. 
\end{proof}
\begin{remark}
  \leavevmode
\vspace{-4pt}
