    By Theorem \cite[Prop. 1.1.11]{BBD}, there always exists a good morphism $g$ completing the commutative diagram \eqref{eq:ABcomdiag} to a morphism of distinguished triangles \eqref{eq:mortrian}.  In all of the situations above, there is a unique morphism $g$, so this is always the case. 
\end{proof}


