    Let $f : [\NN]^2 \to 2$ be a computable coloring. For every $n,k \in \NN$, if $f$ avoids the $k$-fractal of dimension $n$, then every $\emptyset'$-DNC degree $\dbf$ computes an infinite $f$-homogeneous set.
