\section{Social Trading Platforms} \label{supp:website}
A social trading platform is built on the idea of social learning--the notion that the collective wisdom of many traders can outperform the insights of a single individual. Platforms like \textit{ZuluTrade}, \textit{eToro}, and \textit{Darwinex} leverage this concept by allowing users to trade independently or follow and copy the strategies of other successful traders. But this idea extends far beyond trading---it also influences how people interact on social media, citation networks, streaming platforms, and more. That’s why understanding the dynamics within these systems is both important and necessary.
