\section{Data} \label{supp:data}

Our dataset comes from the company eToro and consists of a set of trades from the eToro website. The dataset was preprocessed and prepared in \cite{krafft_bayesian_2021,krafft2016rational}. The dataset contains two tables, one for each trade (top) and one for each of the mirroring relationships (see Table~\ref{supp:data:table:trades}). Each trade is identified by the id of the trader placing that order {\tt CID}, the id for the trader that originated that order {\tt parentCID} (if that trade is mirrored, otherwise 0), the time the order was opened/closed {\tt openDate/closeDate}, the volume of currency traded {\tt unitsDecimal}, the open rate for the traded currency {\tt openRate}, and the net profit from the trade {\tt nProfit}, see \cite{krafft_bayesian_2021}.

